# Recommendation Serving API with ZGC (Java 17+, low-latency experiment)
#
# Use when p99 latency is more important than maximum throughput. ZGC keeps most
# marking/relocation concurrent, so request threads see much shorter STW pauses
# than a heavily pressured G1 heap, at the cost of extra CPU and memory headroom.
-Xms512m
-Xmx1024m
-Xss512k
-XX:SoftMaxHeapSize=768m
-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=256m
-XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=128m
-XX:MaxDirectMemorySize=128m
-XX:+UseZGC
-XX:ZUncommitDelay=300
-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:HeapDumpPath=logs/recsys-serving-zgc.hprof
-XX:ErrorFile=logs/hs_err_recsys-serving-zgc_pid%p.log
-Xlog:gc*,safepoint:file=logs/gc-recsys-serving-zgc-%p.log:time,uptime,level,tags:filecount=5,filesize=20M
